round surrounds one 8-connected foreground outline.\n- The outline is the unique largest foreground color.\n- One or more smaller interior colors are inside the outline; the marker color\n  is the unique smallest non-outline color.\n\nRule:\n- Erase all original foreground pixels to background.\n- Paint every background pixel that is 4-adjacent to the outline with the\n  marker color.\n- Keep the grid shape unchanged.\n\nKey insight: The colored interior marker supplies the paint color, while the\nlargest outline supplies only the contour whose outside edge is traced.\n</description>\n<annotation>\n{\n  \"type\": \"transform_in_place\",\n  \"src\": \"one 8-connected largest foreground outline object and smaller interior marker colors on a dominant background\",\n  \"transform\": \"erase all original foreground pixels; repaint the background pixels 4-adjacent to the outline with the unique smallest non-outline marker color\"\n}\n</annotation>\n</reference_puzzle>\n\n<reference_puzzle rank=\"2\" source=\"eval\" puzzle_id=\"88e364bc\">\n<similarity>\nscore=0.3387\nmechanism=0.4188\nlexical=0.0125\ncode_feature=0.4286\noverlap_tags=code:bbox, code:bfs, code:connected_components, object:closed_region, object:grid_edge, object:marker, object:rectangle, relation:adjacent, relation:direction, relation:inside, relation:row_col\n</similarity>\n<paths>\ncode=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/eval/88e364bc.py\nannotation=/home/lixinyu/snap/new/annotations/88e364bc.json\n</paths>\n<description>\nSlide yellow pixels inside walled regions in the direction dictated by border-legend arrows.\n\nInput structure:\n- bg = most common color; yellow pixels sit inside enclosed regions bounded by colored walls.\n- Border legends: small rectangles on the grid edge whose fill color C matches a region's border color. Each legend contains a center dot and an indicator dot encoding a direction.\n\nRule:\n- For each enclosed region, identify its border color C and look up the legend with fill color